{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and serene gardens. My recent trip lived up to every expectation and then some!\n\nI started in Tokyo, a whirlwind of neon lights, incredible food, and polite crowds. Shibuya Crossing was a must-see – a chaotic ballet of pedestrians! I spent hours exploring quirky shops in Harajuku and indulging in ramen that was, quite simply, life-changing.\n\nNext, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto. The contrast was stunning. Here, history whispered from every corner. I wandered through the breathtaking Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates, and found peace in the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove.  A traditional tea ceremony was a highlight, offering a moment of quiet reflection.\n\nFood was a constant adventure. From delicate sushi and fresh sashimi to savory okonomiyaki, every meal was a delight.  I even braved a vending machine for hot corn soup – surprisingly delicious!\n\nNavigating the language barrier was challenging, but the kindness and helpfulness of the Japanese people made it easy.  I got delightfully lost a few times, but always found my way back with a smile. \n\nJapan is a country of contrasts – ancient traditions seamlessly blended with modern innovation. It’s a place that stays with you long after you leave.  I can't wait to go back!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0013467537937685847}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.17980898916721344}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0014117523096501827}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.16973236203193665}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.12095289677381516}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.20952914655208588}, {"toke